{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792154441000-engineer-6d-a-r2-opus.report.md /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-6d-a/collab/1792163000000-engineer-6da-cljdfix.report.md'","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-16 13:22:29 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-16 20:22:29 +07\nCoding-Agent: claude\nSession-ID: dc3e4b88-02d8-428d-b938-541541f0fbe1\n# Slice 6d-a round 2 (continued): opus takeover, finished on codex's partial diff\n\nRole: VM Runtime. Branch `srvm-6d-a`, base `b9103797`, worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-6d-a`. Model: claude-opus-5-5. Nothing was committed, pushed, or merged. No `src/yang` or `test/yang` file was touched. No collab file is staged. Fable's diff-confirm and sign-off remain outstanding.\n\n## What I found on takeover\n\nCodex's round-2 turn got further than its round-1 report says. When its quota cut it off, it had already:\n- regenerated the ledger golden and written the inventory;\n- applied the layout-gate ruling, so `static-layouts-at-every-pc` was 1783/0;\n- added most of the item 1–13 tests;\n- run a 19-mutant implementation-weakening campaign;\n- partly audited the docs.\n\nMy first focused run (`target/6da/r3-focused-0.log`: 203 tests, 23,371 assertions) had exactly **one** failure: row 20's pin `[{:pc 0 :obligations #{s}}]`. The measurement gave three leading excluded boundaries. The slow tier had never completed, the per-case counts were printed but not pinned, and two driver coverage classes were never reached.\n\n## ATTRIBUTION\n\n| Authored by | Files / hunks |\n|---|---|\n| **codex gpt-6.1-sol (inherited, unchanged by me)** | All of `src/cljc/yin/vm/{engine,semantic}.cljc`, `semantic/{frame,layout}.cljc`, `ucf/rows.cljc`; all of `test/yin/vm/{engine_test,malformed_rows}.cljc`, `semantic/{frame_test,layout_test,vm_test}.cljc`, `ucf/{rows_test,rows_custody_test}.cljc`; both fixtures `test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/{rows-checkpoint-v3,ledger-v2}.txt`; `docs/agents/known-gaps.md`, `yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md`, `yin.vm.semantic.md`, `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md`, `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md`; every `safepoint_harness_test.cljc` hunk not listed below; the codex part of the docs listed below; every `target/6da/r1-*`/`r2-*` artifact |\n| **opus (this turn)** | `safepoint_harness_test.cljc`: (a) the row-20 pin now carries the measured `[pc 0, 1, 2] × #{s}`; (b) a new general check: obligations are unanswered at each excluded boundary and answered at the first measured one; (c) `boundary-description` `:store-keys` also counts installing modules' exports, matching `rows/discharge!`'s answer order (the duplicate key was removed); (d) `quick-boundary-pins`, `quick-boundary-coverage` and their assertions in `sampled-returned-boundaries`; (e) new `running-beside-a-reader`, `two-woken-callers`, `product-driver-cases` and `product-returned-boundaries`; (f) the 89-case pin table and coverage assertion in the slow `every-returned-boundary`; (g) `fn [i p]` → `fn [i _p]` in `structural-sample` (kondo warning) |\n| opus | docs: `yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md` §9 \"refuse unless quiescent\" → holds; `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` §7.6.3 amended marker on \"ready-queue must be empty at lift\"; `yin.vm.dependency-completion.md` §7 amended marker on the `:ready-queue must be empty` clause |\n| opus | `target/6da/r3-*` evidence (logs, measurements, `r3-mutants-test.clj`, `r3-mutation-results.edn`) and this report |\n\nStill flagged for Fable's diff-confirm: the retained-FFI fixture carries the actual wait entry's `:call-id` (`:parked-0`), not nil. This is codex's correction and I kept it.\n\n## What I STOPPED on\n\nNothing. One deviation from a ruling's literal text, resolved under \"carry the actual value and record it\":\n\n- **Row 20's excluded set is 3 boundaries, not 1.** Ruling 2 says \"row 20's excluded set is exactly `[S₀, obligations #{s}]`\". Measured, the setup batch's first `s/def!` stores `s` only after pcs 0, 1 and 2. All three boundaries refuse `[:yin.k/unsatisfied :incomplete]` with obligations exactly `#{s}` and zero serves. They form a contiguous leading run, and every later boundary lifts. That is the ruling's general rule and acceptance item 7's own criterion (\"lifts only from the first boundary at which its definitions are answered in the store\").\n  - The pre-existing `conservative-prefixes-refuse-before-serving` test (codex) pins the same three prefixes independently.\n  - My new assertions prove the cause: `s` is absent at each excluded boundary and present at the first measured one.\n  - `discharge!` is unchanged.\n  - Item 7's doc text keeps the ruling's verbatim \"the leading boundary\" wording. **Fable/acting Architect: confirm or re-word.**\n- **Row 17 is a \"like case\".** Excluded runs, all with obligation `#{host.mod/f}`, answered once the `require` of `host.mod` installs: bare 16, operand 18, depth-3 31, captured 43. Note that in row 17 captured, excluded boundaries (43) outnumber measured ones (27). The obligation is defined by the module the case's own program requires, not by a store `def!`. I count that as \"names the case's own program defines later\" (the work order: \"row 20 and any like case\"). Flagged for confirmation.\n\n## Acceptance 1–14: final outcome\n\nPer-var counters come from the final tree (`target/6da/r3-per-var.log`). Pass/fail/error; no var has any failure or error.\n\n| # | Outcome | Evidence (pass counts) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Done | `frame-test/run-state-rules` 13, `worked-example-running-inventory` 48, `delivery-and-running-windows-are-distinct` 5 |\n| 2 | Done | `rows-test/run-row-slot-and-reference-kinds` 5, `completion-outcome-slot-matrix` 84, `completion-try-and-update-refusals` 16, `task-products-and-ready-validation` 36, `ready-site-mismatch-and-halted-product` 6, `completed-put-history-and-shape-only-ids` 20; all lower refusals assert zero attaches. Mutant campaign below. |\n| 3 | Done | `illegal-task-product-matrix` 30, `running-task-round-trip-and-fencing` 32, `halted-with-outstanding-waits-is-normalized-separately` 8, `a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-carried` 4 |\n| 4 | Done | `completed-link-and-install-outcomes` 48, `completed-link-request-and-active-completions` 32 (zero appends: the retired envelope is never re-appended) |\n| 5 | Done | `shared-cursor-independent-continuations` 9 (independent source vs receiver continuation equality, ordered update bodies), plus the update-body case in `ready-value-portability-and-independent-update-body` 8 |\n| 6 | Done | `rows-custody-test/exclusive-completed-write-is-history` 10, `terminal-completed-write-raises-the-same-outcome` 21 (identity-normalized diagnostic), `completed-ffi-append-becomes-a-response-wait` 8, `completed-poll-observation-is-an-ordinary-read-outcome` 7 |\n| 7 | Done (JVM) | Quick: `sampled-returned-boundaries` **13,755** (23 cases; per-case `[measured excluded park halt]` and coverage pinned). `product-returned-boundaries` **850** (driver from constructed starts; reaches `:active-plus-waits` and `:active-plus-ready`, which no corpus row reaches). Slow: `every-returned-boundary`, 89 cases, per-case counts pinned: **129,274 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors** on the final tree (`r3-slow-final.log`; the measurement run `r3-slow-measure.log` predates the pins). Per point: lift, lower into an isolated world, immediate relift equality (law 2), law 6, window tampers (`check-window-tampers`), isolated law-1 continuation to the reference. Leading exclusions: see STOPPED. |\n| 8 | Done | Structural sampler (5 named samples) across all 22 bare rows plus unwrapped row 20; every boundary for rows 1 and 20 and for the products; `pre-branch-ghost-is-conservatively-unsatisfied` 4; existing cursor/capture/nil/hold cases still green in the quick tier |\n| 9 | Done | `layout-test/static-layouts-at-every-pc` 1783 (ruling-1 gates, enumerated dead-ambient exclusion with asserted cause), `executed-ordered-regions` 66 |\n| 10 | Done | `long-and-nested-initializer-transfers` 1799 (≤ n per task and ≤ n×t per invocation), `engine-test/budgeted-install-children` 11 |\n| 11 | Done | `fuel-counts-instruction-transitions` 80, `bounded-bridge-calls-return` 47, `fuel-dispatch-and-diagnostic-bridge-are-bounded` 4, `fuel-and-closed-gates` 16 |\n| 12 | Done | `running-plus-ready-fenced-recovery` 36 (no-guest/no-scheduler/no-bridge counters, unchanged state, byte-equal relift, `:exporting` and `:ended`) |\n| 13 | Done | `ready-portability-root-oracle` 23 (state/outcome/descriptor roots, independent oracle), `ready-value-portability-and-independent-update-body` 8 |\n| 14 | JVM part done | Kondo 0/0 on all 13 changed Clojure files. Focused namespaces (engine, frame, layout, safepoint-harness, vm, rows, rows-custody, ledger): **218 tests, 24,342 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors** (`r3-focused-final.log`). Whole JVM quick tier `clojure -M:test -e :slow`: **4,079 tests, 269,020 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors** (`r3-quick.log`). Node, Dart and three-host slow runs are the orchestrator's, **not run**. |\n\n## Mutant campaign (implementation-weakening, via `with-redefs`)\n\n- **Codex, 19 mutants, all killed** (`target/6da/r2-mutation-results.edn`, script `r2-mutation-campaign.clj`; baseline 359/0/0). It covers frame rules `:frame-shape :pc-kind :pc-bounds :window-scope :window-extra :window-missing :pending-presence`; row rules `:row-shape :reference-kind :slot-kind :duplicate-key :missing-cursor-cell`; completion site, boolean try, status/refusal, op-id shape; install phase/child kind; task kind table; closed gate. It ran at 19:19, after the last `src` edit (rows.cljc 19:17); `src` is unchanged since.\n- **Opus, 4 more mutants for the execution/backend rules, all killed** (`target/6da/r3-mutation-results.edn`, script `r3-mutants-test.clj`; baseline 1,988/0/0):\n\n| Mutant | Fail / error |\n|---|---|\n| ready roots skipped by `lower-defect` | 15 fail |\n| run-fuel restarts execution after a bridge result | 52 fail |\n| children run unbudgeted (`vm/run`) in the fuel round | 11 fail |\n| dispatch on `active-continuation?` instead of control presence | 1 fail + 1 error |\n\n## Ledger golden regeneration (ruling 3)\n\n- Regenerated by codex through `ledger-fixtures/render` only (`target/6da/r2-ledger-render.log`).\n- Field-classified old/new inventory: **`target/6da/r2-ledger-diff-inventory.edn`**. Classification `:address-only`.\n- The six frame-byte equalities are journal frames 2, 9, 11, 13, 14 and 15. Every change sits at a `:segment/blake3-…` path (`:datoms i 2` or `:datoms i 2 :yin.k/root`); the 14 other frames are byte-identical.\n- I independently checked the git diff: exactly lines 2 (projection) and 5, 12, 14, 16, 17, 18 (= frames 2, 9, 11, 13–15) changed. No continuation frame pack's own bytes changed.\n- Digests (codex-recorded): projection `419e3aa6…` → `52f8127f…`; golden BLAKE3 `5de18ed0…` → `59a6944d…`. Full values are in the inventory file. I did not recompute the golden BLAKE3.\n- Other re-mints (codex, authorized): rows-checkpoint 52/53 addresses (`fixture-remints.json`); 19 inline task-root pins (`root-remints.txt`).\n\n## Docs audit (item 14)\n\nI re-ran the inventory greps (`safepoint|not-quiescent|Quiesce|quiescent`, kind lists, context lists, `maybe-run`, one-cycle). I amended three remaining normative stale clauses, listed in ATTRIBUTION. Codex's `:running` kind in the tuples kind list was already present.\n\nDeliberately left as-is:\n- **UCF §7.7.4 \"Quiesce\" step 1 and §7.8 lifecycle step 1.** Plan v2.1 §3.8 and 6d-b item 8 assign them to 6d-b.\n- **UCF version-0/1 body map `:blocked | :parked | :halted`** and **v2-amendment's version-2 body map.** These are historical wire versions.\n- **UCF acceptance text \"queued work gives not-quiescent\"** and **continuation §8 phase-6 acceptance lists.** These are historical slice records.\n- **`yin.vm.linker.dht.md` mention of not-quiescent.** Linker-DHT hunks are out of this slice, as in round 1.\n- **`ffi/maybe-run` mentions.** These describe the unchanged unrestricted `vm/run`.\n\nThe plan v2.1 §3.8 checks hold: no normative clause assigns the guard to 6d-b, forbids completed link/install wakes, validates completed installs against live installs, restarts fuel through `maybe-run`, or promises one-cycle hold resolution. The §3.5 dead-ambient sentence and the item 7/9 ruling text are in `yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md`.\n\n## File-to-commit mapping (proposal; nothing committed)\n\n| Commit group | Files |\n|---|---|\n| Runtime/carrier | `src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc`, `semantic.cljc`, `semantic/frame.cljc`, `semantic/layout.cljc`, `ucf/rows.cljc` |\n| Tests and re-minted fixtures | `test/yin/vm/engine_test.cljc`, `malformed_rows.cljc`, `semantic/{frame,layout,safepoint_harness,vm}_test.cljc`, `ucf/{rows,rows_custody}_test.cljc`, `test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/rows-checkpoint-v3.txt`, `test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/ledger-v2.txt` |\n| Docs | `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md`, `yin.vm.semantic.md`, `yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`, `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md`, `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md`, `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md`, `yin.vm.dependency-completion.md`, `docs/agents/known-gaps.md` |\n| Never commit | all `collab/` files (prompts, reports), `target/6da/*` |\n\n## Skipped / not claimed\n\n- Node, Dart and the three-host slow landing run were not executed (orchestrator's lanes).\n- I did not re-run codex's 19-mutant campaign. Its `src` and test inputs are unchanged since it ran.\n- I did not recompute the golden BLAKE3 digests.\n- Every inherited codex hunk is unreviewed by a non-author family. That gate is Fable's diff-confirm.\n\nREADY\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-16 14:40:36 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-16 21:40:36 +07\nCoding-Agent: claude\nSession-ID: dc3e4b88-02d8-428d-b938-541541f0fbe1\n# Slice 6d-a cljd compile fix\n\nRole: VM Runtime. Branch `srvm-6d-a`. The fix is commit **`d5987015`**, \"test(yin.vm.semantic): cljd compile gates for 6d-a harness defns\", appended on top of `2a4fe508`. It was pushed to `origin srvm-6d-a` as a fast-forward; no amend and no force-push.\n\nOnly `test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc` changed. No `src/` file and no `:cljs` gate. `collab/` and `review/` files were left untracked.\n\n## Verified locally: yes\n\nA Dart SDK is available locally (`mise exec -- dart --version`: 3.13.5). I iterated on the lane's exact command:\n\n```\nmise exec -- bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only yin.vm.ucf.rows-test,yin.vm.ucf.rows-custody-test,yin.vm.ucf.rows-checkpoint-test,yin.vm.ucf.ledger-fixture-test,yin.vm.semantic.frame-test,yin.vm.semantic.layout-test,yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test,yin.vm.semantic.vm-test,yin.vm.engine-test,yin.vm-test\n```\n\n| Iteration | Result | Log |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Reproduced shiva's failure: compiling `yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test` hits `Cannot invoke \"clojure.lang.IFn.invoke(Object, Object)\" because \"aliases\" is null` while compiling `(defn check-returned-boundaries …)`. cljd compile failed, exit 1. | `target/6da/r5-cljd-1.log` |\n| 2 | After gating the defn, cljd compiled. The **Dart** compiler then failed: `safepoint-harness-test_test.dart:33851: Error: This expression has type 'void' and can't be used. $UNDERSCORE_$2=t_test.expect(...)`. The generated metadata traced it to source line 2834. | `target/6da/r5-cljd-2.log` |\n| 3 | **Exit 0.** \"Running 10 test files in 8 shards\" … \"+267: All tests passed!\". 267 equals the `deftest` count of the ten namespaces (17 + 6 + 50 + 14 + 54 + 15 + 30 + 16 + 30 + 35), so every namespace ran. | `target/6da/r5-cljd-3.log` |\n\nThis is the quick lane only; `slow/guard` bodies print SKIP on cljd. The final commit was reformatted (whitespace only) after iteration 3. I did not re-run the Dart lane on that reformatted text.\n\n## Per-defn gating inventory\n\n| Form | Failure | Gating |\n|---|---|---|\n| `safepoint_harness_test.cljc` `check-returned-boundaries` | cljd compiler NPE (`aliases` is null) in the IFn reify expansion of a multi-arity defn with a destructuring `fn` | `#?(:cljd (defn check-returned-boundaries [& _] nil) :default (defn check-returned-boundaries …real body…))`, with the comment \"cljd compiler NPE on multi-arity + destructuring; stub — JVM/cljs use the real body; no cljd caller (gated)\". Its three callers were already `#?(:cljd nil …)`. The two now-redundant inner `#?(:cljd (throw …) :default (with-redefs …))` were folded back to the plain `with-redefs`. The JVM/cljs body is token-identical to the reviewed one; only indentation changed. |\n| `safepoint_harness_test.cljc` `ready-portability-root-oracle`, binding `_ (when (= root :state) (is (seq wkeys)))` | cljd turned the value-position `is` into `$_ = expect(...)` on a void, which Dart rejects | Became `_ (when (= root :state) (is (seq wkeys)) nil)`, with a one-line comment. The same assertion runs on every host; nothing is gated. |\n\nNo other defn in the ten namespaces needed a gate: the lane compiles and passes after these two.\n\n## JVM quick tier\n\n`clojure -M:test -e :slow` on the final tree: **4,079 tests, 269,020 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors** (`target/6da/r5-quick.log`). This matches the required baseline exactly. kondo reports 0 errors and 0 warnings on the touched file, and cljstyle was applied.\n\n## STOPPED on\n\nNothing.\n\nREADY\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
