{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'steps|step-count|fuel|tick' src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | head -35; sed -n '175,218p' test/yin/vm/ucf/ledger_test.cljc; sed -n '60,100p' test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export_test.cljc; sed -n '284,315p' test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export_test.cljc; sed -n '196,221p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1793650000000-architect-6d-plan-v2.report.md\"","aggregated_output":"143:  \"Execute fuel instructions with the activation in locals; nil fuel runs to exit.\"\n144:  [machine fuel]\n149:             E (:env machine) K (or (:k machine) []) fuel fuel]\n150:        (if (and fuel (zero? fuel))\n155:                remaining (when fuel (dec fuel))]\n280:  \"Execute fuel instructions, refusing a closed gate once at entry.\"\n281:  [machine fuel]\n283:  (vm-hot* machine fuel))\n286:(defn run-fuel\n291:    (throw (ex-info \"Fuel must be a positive exact integer\" {:rule :fuel :fuel n})))\n295:            (engine/scheduler-round-fuel machine register-restore #(run-fuel % n)))]\n(def ^:private baseline\n  {:yin.k/kind :blocked\n   :yin.k/occurrence occ\n   :yin.k/arbitration {:dao.stream/identity arb :dao.stream/descriptor {}}\n   :yin.k/next-op-seq 0\n   :yin.k/ops {}})\n\n\n(defn- offered\n  ([] (offered addr-1))\n  ([address] (offered address baseline))\n  ([address b] (custody/offer occ address \"carrier\" b)))\n\n\n(defn- grant\n  ([] (grant \"lease-1\" \"holder-a\"))\n  ([l h]\n   {:dao.lease/status :dao.lease/accepted\n    :dao.lease/lease l\n    :dao.lease/proposal \"p-1\"\n    :dao.lease/subject {:yin.k/occurrence occ}\n    :dao.lease/holder h\n    :dao.lease/duration {:s 30}}))\n\n\n(defn- bound\n  ([] (bound \"lease-1\" \"holder-a\" 0))\n  ([l h e] (custody/bound occ l h e)))\n\n\n(deftest the-fold-records-offers-grants-and-bindings\n  (let [p (fold [(offered)]\n                [(offered addr-2)]\n                [(grant) (bound)])]\n    (is (= {occ {:yin.k/baseline baseline\n                 :yin.k/variants #{addr-1 addr-2}\n                 :yin.k/epoch 0\n                 :dao.lease/lease \"lease-1\"}}\n           (:occurrences p))\n        \"an equal-baseline variant joins its occurrence\")\n    (is (= {\"lease-1\" {:yin.k/occurrence occ\n                       :dao.lease/holder \"holder-a\"\n                       :yin.k/epoch 0\n                       :dao.space/t 2\n\n\n(defn- served-table\n  \"A `serve!` that counts its calls and answers one stable identity per\n   handle.\"\n  []\n  (let [calls (atom 0)\n        table (atom {})]\n    {:calls calls\n     :table table\n     :serve! (fn [h]\n               (swap! calls inc)\n               (or (get @table h)\n                   (let [served {:dao.stream/identity (str \"s\" (count @table))\n                                 :dao.stream/channel {:dao.stream/type :test/channel}}]\n                     (swap! table assoc h served)\n                     served)))}))\n\n\n(defn- counting-handle\n  [calls]\n  (reify\n    stream/IDaoStreamReader\n\n    (cursor\n      [_ _]\n      (swap! calls inc)\n      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok, :dao.stream/cursor ::at})\n\n    (next\n      [_ _]\n      (swap! calls inc)\n      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked})\n\n\n    stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n\n    (append!\n      [_ _]\n      (swap! calls inc)\n      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})\n        (is (= ['foo] (:yin.k/path r)))))\n    (testing \"a refusal leaves the machine as it was\"\n      (is (zero? @calls)))))\n\n\n(deftest an-explicit-park-travels-in-the-record-test\n  (let [m (rs/parked-explicit)\n        {m' :machine record :record} (export/enter m)\n        {:keys [serve!]} (served-table)\n        prepared (export/prepare m' record serve! nil (index))]\n    (is (seq (:parked m)) \"the source holds a parked record\")\n    (is (= (:parked m) (:parked record)) \"the record holds every parked record\")\n    (is (empty? (:parked m')) \"the machine's :parked holds none\")\n    (is (empty? (:wait-set m')))\n    (is (= :ok (:status prepared)) (pr-str prepared))\n    (let [e (export/encode m' (:record prepared))]\n      (is (= :ok (:status e)) (pr-str e))\n      (is (= :parked (:kind e))))\n    (is (= m (:machine (export/abort m' record [] nil)))\n        \"abort restores machine equality\")))\n\n\n(deftest an-install-childs-parked-records-stay-in-the-child-test\n  (let [m (rs/parked-installer)\n        parked {:p0 {:type :parked-continuation :id :p0}}\n        m (assoc-in m [:installs 'host.mod :vm :parked] parked)\n        {m' :machine record :record :as r} (export/enter m)]\n    (is (= :ok (:status r)) (pr-str r))\n    (is (= parked (get-in m' [:installs 'host.mod :vm :parked]))\n        \"the child's parked records are not moved\")\n    (is (not-any? #(contains? (:parked record) %) (keys parked)))))\n\n1. **Holds.** Refuse `:yin.k/non-portable :reason-mismatch` on `unliftable-hold` as today. (The queue refusal at `:1652-1653` is deleted; `:yin.k/not-quiescent` leaves the outcome vocabulary; §3.7 says why holds stay.)\n2. **Kind.** `:running` when `:control` is set; else `:parked` when the value is a parked record the table holds; else `:blocked` when waits or ready are non-empty; else `:halted` when `halted-with-empty-queue?`; anything else (no control, no waits, no queue, not halted) is `:yin.k/non-portable :inconsistent-state` (unreachable by construction; keep the arm).\n3. **Nodes.** `run` = `{:segment (address! seg) :pc pc :env (:env m) :window (select-keys (:window m) (analysis/live a pc)) :k (or (:k m) [])}` through `state-node` (no `:site`, no `:deliver`) and `context!` for discharge (`live-pcs` from `pc`); waits as today (`:1671`); `ready` = for each queue entry, `(node :ready [(node :wait [(state-node ctx e) (pending-node ctx e)]) (lift-value ctx (:value e)) (:status e) (cells-node ctx (:resource-updates e))])`, where `cells-node` runs each update through `cell!` so the census numbers the advanced cell beside its current cell (two positions of one cell id: the task's `:cursor-cells` row holds the current, the ready row the successor; one canonical number per cell id, as the census already aliases shared cells); the task node gets slots 17 and 18.\n4. `validate-frames` judges slot 17 in context `:running` and each slot-18 wait in context `:wait`. The rest of the lift (store, parked, installs, module stores, discharge, requires, `custody-baseline`, emit) is unchanged; the walk is kind-independent, so a `:running` child is lifted by the same function with `role :child`.\n\n**Lower / restore** (`restore-task` `:2253-2268`): a `:running` task restores `:control {:segment local :pc pc} :window W :env E :k (when (seq K) K) :halted? false :blocked? false :value nil :wait-set entries`; `:blocked`/`:parked`/`:halted` as today; every kind restores `:ready-queue` from slot 18 in order, each entry rebuilt as `(assoc wait-entry :value V :status D :resource-updates {local-cell-key cell})` with cell ids mapped through the receiver's fresh keys (the mapping `with-custody`/`restore-task` already keeps for `:yin.k/recovery-cell-ids`). A fenced restore puts the ready list in `:yin.k/recovery-ready` beside `:yin.k/recovery-waits` and leaves `:ready-queue []`. Nothing runs. `vm/run` (or `run-fuel`) then continues: an active root steps from `pc`; an inactive one sweeps, and the first ready entry resumes before any newly woken wait, in carried order.\n\n**`lower-defect`** (`layout.cljc:916-953`): add `(state-prim code run-row [:run])` over slot 17 (window plus lexical bindings plus `K`, as `:act`) and `(state-prim code (first (:slots (first (:slots r)))) [:ready i])` over slot 18; the de Bruijn backends do not carry install children (unchanged refusal `:installs`), so a running **child** is never lowered into a backend.\n\n**`export/kind-of`** (`export.cljc:274-282`): `(some? (:control m)) → :running` first; `header-agrees?` (`:387-399`) already takes the four-key branch for any non-halted kind; `valid-state?` and `recovery-metadata` gain the ready list (zero issue stamps; the ready entries counted and compared on rehydration).\n\n### 3.3 Custody and lifecycle of a running root\n\n**A running root under a lease.** Full custody slot (policy, occurrence, arbitration, next-op-seq, origin on a successor); `accept-grant!` on lower; gate `:running` on restore; offerable by `ledger/offer-defect` (`ledger.cljc:277`) and `grant/offer-decision` (`authority/grant.cljc:74-75`) once both sets list `:running`; `protect!` checks its retained `:put` waits as for a blocked root (there may be some: F2). The restored machine's first effect parks under the gate (`handle-put` `engine.cljc:532-533`, `handle-next`, `ffi/put-request` answering `full`), so the driver performs it; unchanged from a parked root.\n\n**Four outcomes, specified separately.**\n\n1. **Preemption under live tenure** (the normal path). `run-cycle` runs `(run-fuel m0 n)` when `:fuel` is set (§3.4); the slice returns a machine parked, halted, or at a boundary. The cycle continues (replay, emit, reader step) exactly as today; `cycle-result` leaves the phase `:running` and adds `:yin.k/at-boundary true` to the status detail when `(:control m4)` is set. The composition calls `hand-off` (`driver.cljc:1118-1134`) when it wants to export: `arm-exit` → `export/enter` (its `first-refusal` queue check is deleted; holds remain) → the exit steps mint, prepare, encode (`kind :running`), journal the fence, freeze the recovery object, offer. Only a live-tenure holder reaches `exit-mint` (`:1144`). This is the path that closes the owner's invariant for the holder: a long pure computation is interruptible at every `n` instructions and exportable there.\n2. **Tenure dies after a completed slice** (at `:2123`, inside replay/emit/read, or at the next entry's `binding-check`). 6d-b restructures `run-cycle` so each stage's product is assoc'd into the state **before** the next tenure check (`(-> state (assoc :machine m1) require-tenure! …)`), and `step-active`'s catch ends the run on the state it was handed, which now carries the newest completed pure stage. `end-run` gates the machine `:ended` as today; the ended state additionally carries `:yin.k/retained-boundary {:yin.k/pc … :yin.k/segment … :yin.k/steps-since-checkpoint k}` for inspection and diagnostics. **No adoption**: an ended holder holds no tenure, so `exit-mint` refuses, `abort` refuses `:tenure-ended`/`:tenure-unconfirmed`, and the retained bytes are never offered or resumed. Why retention is safe: under the `:running` gate the slice performs no external observation (effects park; FFI requests are retained for the driver), so `m1` is pure local progress; retaining it loses nothing and discloses nothing.\n3. **Expiry and recovery.** The occurrence is regrantable from its **last durable checkpoint**: the pack this holder lowered, or the last successor it published. The successor relowers it (`step-validating` `:2291-2316`, awaiting-grant for a running root as for a blocked one), `accept-grant!` checks the input prefix and `next-op-seq`, and the writer replays retained writes idempotently by op-id (UCF §7.4.3). **Progress since that checkpoint is lost**: pure computation, and effects performed since (they are durable on the streams and will be re-performed only if their op-ids say they were not). Fuel does not repair this; only exporting before the bound does (outcome 1). The documents say so in those words (§3.7).\n4. **Reopen** (`rebuilt-cell`, `reopen-source`): a fenced snapshot of a running root rehydrates with `:control` set and gate `:exporting` (`rows/lower-task {:fenced true}`); `rehydrate-fenced` re-prepares and must reproduce the pack byte for byte (a `:run` frame is a pure function of the restored fields; the ready list likewise). The kernel refuses to step it: `vm-hot` gains the entry guard `(when (contains? #{:exporting :ended} (vm/gate-mode machine)) (fail \"Gate is closed\" …))` before the loop (`semantic.cljc:137`), one map read per call, not per instruction; `run-fuel` inherits it. Today the guard is moot for parked roots (control nil → `scheduler-round`, which observes nothing under a gate); for a running root it is what makes \"the exporting machine is pure data\" (UCF §7.7.4) true.\n\n**Auto-arm before the bound** (decision 3): recommendation is **not in 6d-b**. `hand-off` stays the composition's explicit act (UCF §7.8); `:yin.k/at-boundary` is the signal. A later policy \"arm the exit when remaining tenure is below one renewal interval\" needs only `lease/holding?` and the clock the driver already reads (`:2060-2063`), no clock-to-instruction conversion, and can live in `compose` without touching the carrier.\n\n**Tests (6d-b)**: clock-controlled cuts (a) immediately before the slice, (b) immediately after it (the `:2123` check), (c) in replay, in emit and in the reader step, (d) between two slices at the next entry's `binding-check`, (e) during `exit-mint`/`prepare`/`offer` of a running root; in each: the source is fenced or ended, no effect was performed past the bound, and **either** a durably authorized successor exists (the offer was accepted under live tenure) **or** the recovery checkpoint is the last pack and `:yin.k/retained-boundary` reports the lost steps; byte-equality of `rehydrate-fenced` for a running root with waits and with a ready entry; two competing candidates for a `:running` offer; stale-source stepping refused by the gate guard; `abort` with uncertain offer refused; expired-grant admission refused.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
