{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '430,453p' test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc; sed -n '2400,2445p' test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc; sed -n '438,460p' test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export_test.cljc; rg -n 'defn.*new-machine|source-index' test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc | head -15; sed -n '2650,2670p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc; sed -n '80,110p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md\"","aggregated_output":"    ;; composition links host.mod itself, so its relift discharges host.mod/f.\n    {:machine m :kind :blocked :reason :next :steps [#(stream/append! src \"B\")] :trace (atom [])\n     :receiver (constantly {:opts {:modules (:modules m)}})}))\n\n\n(defn run-beside\n  [m ast]\n  (vm/run (load-program (if (= :semantic (lane-of m)) (assoc m :env (:free-env m)) m) ast)))\n\n\n(defn parking\n  [m]\n  (let [pid (:id (vm/value m))]\n    {:machine m :kind :parked :pid pid :trace (atom [])\n     :resume #(run-beside % {:type :vm/resume :parked-id pid :val (s/lit \"back\")})}))\n\n\n(defn module-store-cursors\n  \"An explicit park whose module store holds two cursor references nothing\n   else reaches, named by a module closure in the task store.\"\n  [wrap]\n  (let [ring (s/ring 4)\n        ast (with-cat (wrap (s/app (s/lam ['p] {:type :vm/park}) (s/lit 1))))\n        v (project ast)\n   [9 :bare] [16 0 0 1] [10 :bare] [21 0 0 1] [11 :bare] [20 0 0 1] [12 :bare] [24 0 0 1]\n   [13 :bare] [10 0 1 1] [14 :bare] [39 0 0 1] [15 :bare] [41 0 0 1] [16 :bare] [51 0 0 1]\n   [17 :bare] [18 16 0 1] [18 :bare] [14 0 1 1] [19 :bare] [7 0 0 1] [21 :bare] [31 0 0 1]\n   [22 :bare] [44 0 0 1] [24 :bare] [10 0 2 1] [20 :unwrapped] [13 3 0 2]})\n\n\n(def quick-boundary-coverage\n  #{:body-entry :taken-branch :untaken-branch :jump :non-tail-call :return :tail-transition\n    :capture :resume :park :ffi-park :running-install-child})\n\n\n(defn running-beside-a-reader\n  \"Active control beside an outstanding reader wait. The beside activation\n   blocks on its own stream before either answer arrives, so both waits\n   wake in one sweep and no boundary halts beside an outstanding wait (that\n   normalization is pinned separately).\"\n  []\n  (let [src (s/ring 4) other (s/ring 4)\n        [sref m] (engine/attach-resource (machine) src)\n        [cref m] (engine/handle-cursor m {:stream sref} :reader-cursor)\n        [oref m] (engine/attach-resource m other)\n        [dref m] (engine/handle-cursor m {:stream oref} :beside-cursor)\n        reader (vm/run (load-program (assoc m :store {'c cref 'd dref}) (s/then read-op read-op)))\n        _ (stream/append! src \"A\")\n        reader (vm/run reader)]\n    {:machine (load-program (assoc reader :env (:free-env reader))\n                            (s/then (s/app (s/v '+) (s/lit 1) (s/lit 2)) (s/next-of (s/v 'd))))\n     :steps [(fn [] nil) #(do (stream/append! src \"B\") (stream/append! other \"C\"))] :trace (atom [])}))\n\n\n(defn two-woken-callers\n  \"Two waits on one continuation, both answered: the first resume runs\n   beside the second's queued outcome.\"\n  []\n  (let [call-in (s/ring 8) call-out (s/ring 8)\n        m (vm/run (load-program (machine {:call-in call-in :call-out call-out\n                                          :call-out-cursor (vm/mint-oldest call-out :test)})\n                                (s/call-node :op/echo \"hello\")))\n        e1 (first (:wait-set m))]\n    {:machine (assoc m :wait-set [e1 (assoc e1 :call-id :parked-9)])\n     :steps [#(answer-both! call-out (:call-id e1))] :trace (atom [])}))\n\n\n(def product-driver-cases\n  \"Constructed starts the stepping driver runs from, for the §3.6 classes\n   no corpus row reaches: [id segment expected build].\"\n\n(deftest the-recovery-object-is-the-pack-and-holder-local-state-test\n  (let [{:keys [frozen prepared machine]} (frozen-of (rs/parked-explicit))\n        recovery (cbor/decode (:bytes frozen))\n        published (export/encode machine (:record prepared))]\n    (is (= :ok (:status frozen)) (pr-str frozen))\n    (is (= #{:yin.k/export-recovery :yin.k/version :yin.k/pack-address :yin.k/root\n             :yin.k/pack-bytes :yin.k/header :yin.k/state}\n           (set (keys recovery)))\n        \"one body: no snapshot, no descriptors (the pack carries them)\")\n    (is (= 2 (:yin.k/version recovery)))\n    (is (= (:address published) (:pack-address frozen) (:yin.k/pack-address recovery)))\n    (is (= (:root published) (:root frozen) (:yin.k/root recovery)))\n    (is (= (vec (:bytes published)) (vec (:pack-bytes frozen))\n           (vec (jing/base64->bytes (:yin.k/pack-bytes recovery)))))\n    (is (jing/segment-bytes-match? (:address frozen) (:bytes frozen)))\n    (is (= #{:gate :origins :issues :issued :children} (set (keys (:yin.k/state recovery)))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Rehydrate: fenced, reproducible, without program IO\n;; =============================================================================\n\n53:(def source-index\n75:    (swap! source-index update a (fnil conj #{}) (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast]))\n201:  {:source-index @source-index})\n990:          d (error #(rows/lift-task (:machine world) (:serve! (served #{:reader})) {:source-index {}}))]\n           :restart-checkpoint {:bytes origin-bytes :address (:address origin-fence)}\n           :status :yin.k/ok\n           :detail {:reopened :exit :yin.k/occurrence o1}\n           :occurrence o1\n           :arbitration (get-in cell [:header :yin.k/arbitration\n                                      :dao.stream/identity])\n           :lease l\n           :machine nil\n           :exit (cond-> cell\n                   (nil? report-intent) (dissoc :report)\n                   (some? report-intent)\n                   (assoc :report\n                          {:request (assoc (:yin.k/request report-intent)\n                                           :yin.k/bytes (:bytes cell))\n                           :sent true\n                           :answer (when (contains? (:acked folded)\n                                                    report-rid)\n                                     (get-in folded [:answers report-rid\n                                                     :yin.k/answer]))}))\n           :release (when (some? release-intent)\n                      {:lease l\nfs/walk-file-tree or .listFiles; each string literal argument of its\nio/file, fs/file, fs/path, fs/glob, java.io.File. or File. calls is a root\n(let-bound roots count), and a change under a root selects it. The three\nlanes run in parallel (logs: target/profile/changed-<lane>.log) after the\nneeded builds. `test:changed:list` shows what and why; `:clj`/`:cljs`/\n`:cljd` run one lane; `--base REF`; `--changed FILE...` (absolute OK; a\ntypo, an empty list or the wrong cwd exits 1). Use it to iterate and to\nland a slice confined to a package. Exit 2 (from :list too) is a wide\nchange (deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn mise.toml .cljstyle src/dev/\nantlr/ .clj-kondo/ package*/pubspec*): it runs nothing; run `bb test`,\nas for a change to the core everything requires (yin.vm engine,\ndao.stream, codecs) and before a big merge. Not seen: dynamic loads\n(`requiring-resolve`, `resolve`), paths or walk roots built at run time,\nand spawned programs that changed (target/yin-repl.js, Dart peers).\n\n### Subsystem-first tests: `bb test:sub`\n\n`bb test:sub <subsystem>...` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the tests belonging to\none or more canonical subsystems (defined in `src/dev/subsystems.edn`). Selection\nis by longest namespace prefix matching.\n\n```sh\nbb test:sub <subsystem>...        # All three lanes in parallel (fast form)\nbb test:sub:clj <subsystem>...    # JVM lane alone\nbb test:sub:cljs <subsystem>...   # Node lane alone\nbb test:sub:cljd <subsystem>...   # Dart lane alone\nbb test:sub:list <subsystem>...   # Show namespaces, builds, Class B seams & dependents; runs nothing\nbb test:sub <subsystem>... --slow # Include slow tests (-i :slow on JVM, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1 on Node/Dart)\nbb -cp src/dev -m affected-test   # Run affected-test self-tests directly in Babashka\n```\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
