{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '370,428p' test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/reader_test.cljc; sed -n '428,461p' test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/reader_test.cljc; sed -n '715,744p' test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver_test.cljc; rg -n '\"'^FAIL|''^ERROR|''^Ran|failures,.*errors|Syntax error'\"' target/6db/compose-1.log | head -25; sed -n '310,362p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792145566000-architect-6d-plan-v21.report.md\"","aggregated_output":"          \"the entry is not applied before the acknowledgment\")\n      (is (= [:observe] (mapv :reason (:wait-set (:machine r1))))\n          \"it still waits\")\n      (is (= 0 (get-in (:machine r1) [:yin.k/custody :input :next]))\n          \"k has not advanced\"))\n    (testing \"the request is the input protocol's, with the source inside :yin.k/name\"\n      (is (= {:yin.k/request :yin.k/input\n              :yin.k/request-id [:yin.k/input \"lease-1\" 0]\n              :yin.k/input {:yin.k/occurrence occ\n                            :dao.lease/lease \"lease-1\"\n                            :yin.k/epoch 0\n                            :yin.k/input-seq 0\n                            :yin.k/source (read-source :poll []\n                                                       (stream-id h)\n                                                       position)\n                            :yin.k/observed observed}}\n             (:request (first (:appended r1))))\n          \"no cell id, host cursor or sealed reference anywhere\"))\n    (testing \"the held observation rides the entry in state 2\"\n      (is (= {:yin.k/input-seq 0\n              :yin.k/source (read-source :poll [] (stream-id h) position)\n              :yin.k/observed observed\n              :yin.k/state :requested}\n             (get-in (:machine r1) [:wait-set 0 :yin.k/held]))))\n    (testing \"a record that is not the acknowledgment applies nothing\"\n      (let [mallory (reader/settle (:machine r1) \"mallory\"\n                                   {:yin.k/reply :yin.k/input\n                                    :yin.k/request-id [:yin.k/input \"lease-1\" 0]\n                                    :yin.k/answer {:yin.k/status :recorded\n                                                   :yin.k/input-seq 0}})]\n        (is (nil? (:applied mallory)))\n        (is (nil? (:run-end mallory)))\n        (is (empty? (:ready-queue (:machine mallory))))))\n    (testing \"the acknowledged observation applies exactly once\"\n      (answer! w 2)\n      (let [d (reader/drain (:machine r1) (ack-reader w))]\n        (is (= [0] (mapv :input-seq (:applied d))))\n        (is (empty? (:wait-set (:machine d))) \"the poll entry left the wait set\")\n        (is (= [\"A\"] (mapv :value (:ready-queue (:machine d))))\n            \"woken with the poll's own value\")\n        (is (= 1 (get-in (:machine d) [:yin.k/custody :input :next]))\n            \"k advanced exactly once\")\n        (is (nil? (some :yin.k/held (concat (:wait-set (:machine d))\n                                            (:ready-queue (:machine d)))))\n            \"the held state is gone (state 4)\")\n        (testing \"a second acknowledgment of the same k retains\"\n          (let [again (reader/settle (:machine d) arb\n                                     {:yin.k/reply :yin.k/input\n                                      :yin.k/request-id [:yin.k/input \"lease-1\" 0]\n                                      :yin.k/answer {:yin.k/status :recorded\n                                                     :yin.k/input-seq 0}})]\n            (is (nil? (:applied again)))))))\n    (is (= 1 @calls) \"still exactly one live observation across the whole flow\")))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The held-observation rule: one observation, one k, any number of retries\n;; =============================================================================\n(deftest a-held-poll-survives-ten-failed-recording-attempts-test\n(deftest a-held-poll-survives-ten-failed-recording-attempts-test\n\n  (let [h (ring 8)\n        _ (stream/append! h \"A\")\n        [cref parked] (gated-poll h)\n        position (get-in parked [:resources (:id cref) :cursor])\n        observed (stream/next h position)\n        m (assoc parked :yin.k/custody (prefix-custody []))\n        [observe! calls] (counting-observe)\n        dropping (fn [_r] {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error})\n        round (fn [machine] (:machine (reader/step machine dropping observe!)))\n        final (reduce (fn [machine _n] (round machine)) m (range 10))]\n    (is (= 1 @calls) \"ten failed recordings, one observation\")\n    (is (= 1 (count (:wait-set final))) \"the entry still waits\")\n    (is (empty? (:ready-queue final)))\n    (is (= 0 (get-in final [:yin.k/custody :input :next])) \"one k, never advanced\")\n    (is (= {:yin.k/input-seq 0\n            :yin.k/source (read-source :poll [] (stream-id h) position)\n            :yin.k/observed observed\n            :yin.k/state :requested}\n           (get-in final [:wait-set 0 :yin.k/held]))\n        \"the exact observation is retained through every failure\")\n    (testing \"the eleventh attempt that lands still sends the same request\"\n      (let [w (world)\n            r (reader/step final (appender w) observe!)]\n        (is (= 1 @calls) \"the observation was not repeated\")\n        (is (= {:yin.k/input-seq 0\n                :yin.k/source (read-source :poll [] (stream-id h) position)\n                :yin.k/observed observed\n                :yin.k/state :requested}\n               (get-in (:machine r) [:wait-set 0 :yin.k/held])))))))\n\n\n(deftest a-full-append-leaves-the-request-unsent-test\n\n\n(deftest paused-grant-and-delayed-activation-test\n  (doseq [expired? [false true]]\n    (let [{:keys [sources]} (reader-source)\n          world' (world :holders [\"holder-a\"] :sources sources)\n          accepted (split-grant world' sources)\n          state (:state accepted)]\n      (is (= :activating (:phase state)))\n      (is (nil? (:machine state)))\n      (is (zero? @(:attaches accepted)))\n      (reset! (:clock accepted) (if expired? {:s 31} {:s 2}))\n      (let [resumed (driver/program-step state)]\n        (if expired?\n          (do (is (= :releasing (:phase resumed)))\n              (is (zero? @(:attaches accepted)))\n              (is (nil? (:machine resumed))))\n          (do (is (= :running (:phase resumed)))\n              (is (pos? @(:attaches accepted)))\n              (is (= {:s 1} (get-in resumed [:holder :granted-at])))))))))\n\n\n(defn- inbox-obstructed-tick\n  [state split?]\n  (if split?\n    (driver/program-step (driver/control-step state))\n    (driver/step state)))\n\n\n(deftest unavailable-outcomes-preserve-renewal-and-suspend-program-test\n\nLet:\n\n```text\nregister-sequence(p) = layout(p) ++ uses-in-order(p)\nexpected-values(p)   = [W[r] for r in register-sequence(p)]\n```\n\nAfter the separately specified dead-prefix treatment, compare the kernel region to `expected-values(p)` in emitter order. Its length equals the length of `register-sequence(p)`. Repeated occurrences of a virtual register occupy repeated positions and must decode to agreeing values.\n\nSeparately check:\n\n```text\nset(layout(p)) ∪ set(uses(p)) = L(p)   at reachable non-tail PCs\nset(uses(p))                 = L(p)   at reachable tail-call PCs\n```\n\nThere is no requirement that the length of the ordered sequence equal `|L(p)|`. Static checks validate layout availability and register sets; dynamic checks validate actual region length, order and repeated-register agreement.\n\n**Change:** Consensus P2-6 removes the false cardinality equation without weakening ordered reconstruction.\n\n**Dead ambient operands (static domain).** The non-tail set equation holds where the enclosing application's pending reads are still reachable. At the operand PCs of an application whose evaluation an operand-position tail call or `:resume` abandons (the corpus's `:resume-operand` and `:tail-operand` fixtures), ambient layout entries are dead per L while remaining in the region: the strongest static truth there is the inclusion `uses(p) ⊆ L(p) ⊆ layout(p) ∪ uses(p)`; the equality is permanently excluded at those pcs. 6e's dead-prefix rule governs the region after the transfer, and 6e's ordered dynamic checks — not the static set equality — carry those pcs.\n\n### 3.6 Harness order, worlds, oracle, coverage\n\n**Replace the coverage and refusal-oracle paragraphs; retain v2’s lift → lower → immediate relift → law 6 → execution order and isolated worlds.**\n\n**Coverage.**\n\nThe stepping driver uses returned `run-fuel 1` boundaries. Its coverage classes are body entry, taken and untaken branch, jump, non-tail call, return, tail transition, capture, resume, park, FFI park, active-plus-waits, active-plus-ready, and running install child.\n\nBlocked-plus-ready is tested through an explicit **post-sweep/pre-resume fixture**, constructed with `check-wait-set`. It is not a mandatory returned boundary of the stepping driver. The shared-cursor fixture uses this same seam.\n\nReport driver coverage separately from constructed scheduler-product coverage. Pin per-case/per-host counts after measurement. Neither coverage inventory claims a theorem over all programs.\n\n**Refusal oracle.**\n\nThe independent test traversal covers:\n\n- Run windows and lexical bindings.\n- Every K-frame window and lexical binding.\n- Outstanding wait delivery states.\n- Ready delivery states and ready outcome values.\n- Optional ready refusal values and restored value-bearing completion fields.\n- Parked states and recursively reached collections, closures and continuations.\n\nFor register targets, exactly the expected unsupported points refuse `:yin.k/unsupported :continuation-registers` before attachment. Every other point in the admitted backend fragment transfers and continues to the reference outcome. Include a case whose only unsupported primitive is nested in a queued outcome.\n\nTerminal outcomes are compared as outcomes: receiver and source must raise the same classified failure with the same portable diagnostic data after identity normalization, rather than both being required to return a guest value.\n\n**Change:** Consensus P2-7; muse N4/glm O3; glm’s terminal-status acceptance omission.\n\n### 3.7 Amended document text\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
