\n  \"Decide the offer of variant `address` with baseline `b` on `medium`\n   against projection p.\"\n  [address medium b]\n  (fn [p]\n    (let [o (:yin.k/occurrence b)\n          known (get-in p [:occurrences o])\n          succession (when-not known (completion/offer-refusal p address b))]\n      (cond\n        (or (:yin.k/fork b)\n            (not (contains? #{:running :blocked :parked} (:yin.k/kind b))))\n        (reply :refused :not-offerable nil)\n        (not (custody/occurrence? o))\n        (reply :refused :malformed-occurrence nil)\n        (not= (:arbitration p)\n              (get-in b [:yin.k/arbitration :dao.stream/identity]))\n        (reply :refused :foreign-arbitration o)\n        (nil? medium) (reply :refused :missing-medium o)\n        (contains? (:yin.k/variants known) address)\n        {::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :replayed :yin.k/occurrence o}}\n        (and known (not= (:yin.k/origin b)\n           :kondo {:extra-deps {clj-kondo/clj-kondo {:mvn/version \"2026.01.19\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"clj-kondo.main\"]}\n           :dbg {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                 :main-opts [\"-m\" \"debug-cljd\"]\n                 :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :cljd-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.runner\"]}\n           :cljd-yin-repl-build\n           {:main-opts  [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n            :cljd/opts  {:kind       :dart\n                         :main       yin.repl.main\n                         :output-dir \"build/yin-repl\"\n                         :output-to  \"build/yin-repl/yin_repl.dart\"}}\n           :dep-graph {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                       :extra-deps {org.clojure/tools.namespace {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}}\n                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"dep-graph\"]}}}\n\n\n;; clj -X:fmt\n\n;; clj -M:nREPL\n\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:135:(defn- check-gate!\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export.cljc:400:(defn- valid-state?\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc:178:(defn- check-common!\n797: [sp :yin.safepoint/use          #{…}]                   ; registers read at this pc (static, from A)\n798: [sp :yin.safepoint/live         #{…}]                   ; L(pc) (static, from A)\n799: [sp :yin.safepoint/lexically-required [x conn]]         ; names this pc can read from E (static)\n800: [sp :yin.safepoint/layout       {…}]]                   ; engine-owned: physical location → virtual register (continuation design §4)\n812:- `:yin.safepoint/layout` is opaque to the protocol. It is a memo the engine\n819:- A request to lift at a pc outside every body returns `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` naming the pc; the name is historical, the meaning is \"no state of A exists here\". A stack image's `:push` pc is relabelled to its successor's A pc without running anything. An engine may not invent states a record does not have, and two engines that disagree about the state set of one address are not both conforming. An engine that cannot hold a value of the canonical frame refuses before attachment with its own kind (the register backend's `:continuation-registers`); that is a limit of the engine, not of the address.\n821:A debugger's breakpoint set is any subset of the pcs of A; the safepoint set is where the program will stop by itself.\n925:safepoint of the same name (`yin.vm.linker.md` 7.2, 7.3). A wait entry's\n1044:  quiescence requirements, with kind `:blocked`, `:parked`, or\n1048:  a blocked child is valid. A runnable, non-quiescent child refuses\n1673:  (`:yin.k/not-quiescent` otherwise, §7.4.1) — a task with queued runnable\n1678:  quiescence refusal.\n2628:   else `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`; canonicalize every referenced segment and\n2690:| `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` | lift | `:yin.k/segment`, `:yin.k/pc`: the pc is outside every body of A |\n3123:  `:yin.safepoint/kinds`, `def`/`use`/`live`, and lexical reads agree with\n3128:  reproduce the canonical frame. A pc outside every body gives `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`;