{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_83","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1034,1057p' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md; sed -n '615,629p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1793650000000-architect-6d-plan-v2.report.md; rg -n 'safepoint|not-quiescent|three kinds|:blocked :parked' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export.cljc; cat mise.toml | head -40; rg -n '\"'^##'\"' docs/agents/build-n-test.md | head -15\"","aggregated_output":"  else lift refuses `:yin.k/non-portable`, kind `:install-response`.\n- A response is verified by the resumer, not trusted because it\n  decodes. Its manifest names the module the entry is keyed by, its\n  link id equals `:yin.k/parent`, and its image and manifest pass the\n  checks the linker applied at delivery (`yin.vm.linker.md` sections\n  5 and 9): the image is well formed, hashes to the address it is\n  delivered under, and is the image the manifest names. A failure is\n  `:yin.k/undecodable` naming the entry's response.\n- A live install entry carries phase `:running` or `:parked`. Its\n  child independently satisfies the handoff grammar and the\n  quiescence requirements, with kind `:blocked`, `:parked`, or\n  `:halted`. The phase records scheduler progress; it does not\n  substitute for validation of the child's actual machine state,\n  and no phase requires or forbids a kind: a `:running` phase with\n  a blocked child is valid. A runnable, non-quiescent child refuses\n  export. Lower preserves both fields, and the scheduler continues\n  from the restored child without rerunning initialization. Other\n  install phases are not exportable live-child entries, and any\n  other phase value is `:yin.k/undecodable`. No stricter relation\n  between phase and kind is introduced until a scheduler\n  normalization invariant is specified and proved; M-next D tests\n  every combination of the two phases and three kinds, explicit\n  park included.\n- The resumer restores the child's carried state into the fresh\n### 3.11 Risks\n\n1. **A liveness bug surfaces** at a pc no park looked at: law 1 fails there. A finding, not a slice risk; the main reason to run the every-boundary laws.\n2. **The ready carrier meets a wake reason I did not enumerate** (a link wake entering the queue): pinned as `:ready-reason` refusal in 6d-a and reported; widening is a small follow-up, not a redesign.\n3. **Re-mint churn**: two re-mints in a week (module-pins, 6d-a). Mitigation: order (§3.9); 6d's own acceptance pins boundary counts and refusal kinds, never root ids.\n4. **Dead-prefix rule untested on a real case** if the fragment has none: 6e item 6 pins it on a hand-built vector; the rule is then a documented check awaiting a natural case.\n5. **Slow-tier time on Dart**: slow tier only; measured once.\n6. **Gate guard cost**: one map read per `run-fuel`/`vm-hot` call; a reviewer confirms it is outside the loop.\n7. **Fuel too small or too large**: a composition knob; default nil.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Verification honesty\n\n- Every `file:line` above was read in `7c4dff32` today. The review's citations held in every case I checked; where it cited a function by name I read the body.\n[tools]\njava = [\"21\", \"17\"]\ncljstyle = \"0.17.642\"\nzprint = \"1.3.0\"\nbabashka = \"latest\"\nclojure = \"1.12.4.1602\"\nnode = \"25.6.1\"\nandroid-sdk = \"latest\"\nflutter = { version = \"latest\", platforms = \"\"\"\n[linux-x64]\nurl = \"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/beta/linux/flutter_linux_{{ version }}-beta.tar.xz\"\n\n[macos-arm64]\nurl = \"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/beta/macos/flutter_macos_arm64_{{ version }}-beta.zip\"\n\n[macos-x64]\nurl = \"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/beta/macos/flutter_macos_{{ version }}-beta.zip\"\n\n[windows-x64]\nurl = \"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/beta/windows/flutter_windows_{{ version }}-beta.zip\"\n\"\"\", version_json_path = \".releases[?channel=beta].version\", version_list_url = \"https://storage.googleapis.com/flutter_infra_release/releases/releases_macos.json\" }\n\n[env._]\npath = [\n  \"{{env.HOME}}/.local/share/mise/installs/android-sdk/1.0/platform-tools\",\n  \"{{env.HOME}}/.local/share/mise/installs/android-sdk/1.0/emulator\",\n]\n\n[env]\n#FLUTTER_STORAGE_BASE_URL = \"https://storage.flutter-io.cn\"\n#PUB_HOSTED_URL = \"https://pub.flutter-io.cn\"\n7:## Commands\n73:### Changed-only tests: `bb test:changed`\n95:### Subsystem-first tests: `bb test:sub`\n111:#### Canonical Subsystems (`src/dev/subsystems.edn`)\n124:#### Gate Ladder (docs/design/test.subsystems.md)\n185:## Test tiers: quick and slow\n301:## Remote test servers: shiva and jupiter\n316:### Get the code there: push to origin, never rsync\n337:### Activate the toolchain in the right order\n354:### Which lanes may overlap (reconciling the one-lane-set rule)\n382:### The full run\n432:### Known differences from the laptop\n445:### Measured times (first runs, 2026-10-11, commit 84c7c9b7, all lanes concurrent)\n454:## Testing Philosophy & TDD\n467:## Debugging Malformed CLJ / EDN / CLJS\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
