{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_84","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '793,803p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/compose.cljc; sed -n '838,846p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/compose.cljc; sed -n '1,24p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md; rg -n ':yin.k/steps-since' test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"  [c h config]\n  (add-holder c h config driver/initial))\n\n\n(defn source\n  \"Add the source half: `config` carries :machine -- the machine at its\n   park, halt or instruction boundary, holding no custody -- beside the holder seams of\n   `holder` (no :bytes and :address: the driver mints those).  An\n   exclusive composition offers the export on its own arbitration --\n   the composition names it, and a supplied :arbitration is a refused\n   assembly; a fork composition (the composition's fork decision,\n\n\n(defn hand-off\n  \"The composition's explicit export of holder `h`'s parked continuation\n   (`driver/hand-off`): the exit half arms at the park, halt or instruction boundary the next\n   control and program steps drive to its report, release and closure.\"\n  [c h]\n  (update-in c [:holders h] driver/hand-off))\n\n---\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\n---\n\n# BUILD & TEST\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\nbb test              # All three lanes (JVM, Node, Dart), fast default form: no slow tests\nbb test:all          # Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\nbb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\n# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\nbb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\nbb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\nbb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\nbb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_85","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md');s=p.read_text();a=s.index('- A live install entry carries phase');b=s.index('- The resumer restores',a);s=s[:a]+'''- A live install entry carries phase \"'`:running` with a `:running` child, or phase `:parked` with a `:blocked` child. The child independently satisfies the complete task-product grammar, including ordered completed outcomes. The engine links a halted child in the sweep it halts in. No ready-queue quiescence requirement applies. Lower preserves the carried child without rerunning initialization; receiver module admission remains required before attachment.\n'\"'''+s[b:];s=s.rstrip()+'\\\\n';p.write_text(s)\np=Path('test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver_test.cljc');s=p.read_text().replace('''           (is (= (:bytes state) (:bytes result)) \\\"retained state never replaces the checkpoint\\\")''','''           (is (= (:bytes state) (:bytes result)) \\\"retained state never replaces the checkpoint\\\")\n           (is (= (if (= :before cut) 0 1)\n                  (get-in result [:yin.k/retained-boundary :yin.k/steps-since-checkpoint])))''');p.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
