{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_123","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > collab/1792172314000-engineer-6d-b.report.md <<'MD'\nCreated-GMT: 2026-10-16 17:57:08 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-17 00:57:08 +07\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: 01a145cc-0712-76d1-bd92-811f949312c6\n# Task: slice 6d-b — holder, custody, expiry, recovery for the running root\nRole: VM Runtime\nImplementers:\n- Model: gpt-6.1-sol (dispatch assignment) | Assigned: 2026-10-17 01:25 +07 | Status: implementation complete; final JVM quick-tier result pending | Rationale: holder lifecycle following Fable-signed 6d-a\n\nBranch \"'`srvm-6d-b`, base `73c28036`. The Fable follow-up is committed separately as **262fc609d**. The slice implementation is **uncommitted**, for Fable review. Nothing pushed or merged. No `src/yang`, `test/yang`, protected root/byte pins, or collab file was committed.\n\n## Preconditions and attribution\n\nRead the master architecture, build/test rules, governing plan v2.1 (including inherited v2 clauses), both 6d-a engineer reports, glm/cmd reviews, and Fable'\"'s signed-head confirmation. \"'`mise trust` completed with elevated access because the trust registry is outside this worktree; `npm ci` succeeded. The workspace initially contained only the dispatch prompt as an untracked collab file; no inherited uncommitted implementation was present. The existing 6d-a carrier, run-fuel, gate guards and module admission behavior remain attributed to the signed base, not this slice. The `:store-keys` drift caveat is recorded in known gaps; the acknowledged `receive-module` restoration behavior is unchanged.\n\n## First commit: Fable post-merge follow-ups\n\n**262fc609d — docs(yin.vm): record Fable post-merge 6d-a follow-ups**\n\n- Known-gaps status now says “6d-a landed at d5987015; 6d-b and 6e pending”.\n- Added the honest module-exported-host-function any-pc hole, assigned to 6e or later module-coordinate/host-profile lifting.\n- Temporarily annotated not-quiescent as holder-only; this slice removes that annotation with its queue refusal.\n- Corrected `check-install!`'\"'s docstring to blocked/parked and running/running.\n- Added glm's non-projected-vector comment on the protected zero? layout pin. The assertion/pin is unchanged.\n- Optional timestamp normalization was not performed.\n\n## Per-part implementation\n\n1. **Driver.** \"'`check-common!` accepts nil or positive integer `:fuel`, retained by the constructor and test reopen config. A configured execution uses `(if fuel (sr/run-fuel m0 fuel) (vm/run m0))` under the existing gate/halted guards. Execution, replay, emit and live-read stages return explicit `{:status :ok :state ...}` / `{:status :failed :state ... :failure ...}` outcomes. Each next stage checks tenure against the preceding completed state. The post-cycle drain is similarly guarded. Journal uncertainty and inbox refusal propagate. Failure consumption calls `end-run` with the carried state, preserving the latest completed machine behind `:ended`.\n2. **Diagnostics.** Active control reports `:yin.k/at-boundary true`; no automatic hand-off policy was added. `:yin.k/retained-boundary` is inspection-only and records PC, segment, checkpoint and `:yin.k/steps-since-checkpoint`. **Unit clarification:** the latter counts completed holder execution slices/program steps, not guest instructions. The runner exposes no completed-instruction counter; the documents state the actual unit rather than deriving a false count from fuel, especially for early parks and scheduler trees. A throwing, unreturned stage contributes no invented partial machine.\n3. **Export/recovery.** Removed `first-refusal`; the root'\"'s ordered ready queue moves into the export record and is reinstated for lift/abort. \"'`kind-of` prioritizes running control and recognizes ready-only blocked tasks. Recovery metadata carries/validates ready count, and fenced extraction consumes `:yin.k/recovery-ready` into the retained record. The published pack is reproduced byte for byte. The `abort` function'\"'s authority/uncertainty conditions are unchanged.\n4. **Custody/composition.** Ledger and grant offerability admit running roots, while halted-root refusal remains. Compose admits/forwards holder \"'`:fuel` and `:yin.k/admitted-modules` (the latter is needed for the composed running-install-child transfer). No execution guard was introduced here; the 6d-a guard is reused and integration-tested.\n5. **Documents.** Applied continuation §7.3, UCF exporting/lifecycle/conformance/architectural clauses and linker-DHT §14.1/related handoff text. Replaced Quiesce step 1 with ordered completed-outcome retention. Documents explicitly state last-durable-checkpoint recovery and lost progress. Updated the obsolete UCF child-quiescence paragraph to the already-landed phase/kind rules. Reader documentation and known gaps record arbitrary acknowledgement/backpressure delay.\n6. **Stage E.** Added a fuelled running world, source/receiver hand-off, cuts before and after the successor offer, and expiry between slices. Snapshot summaries expose the fuelled machine as portable inspection data and count serves/attaches/observations; pure running scenarios assert zero. Added the corresponding process matrix test for the orchestrator'\"'s slow landing lane; it was not run here.\n\n## Acceptance evidence\n\nFinal focused JVM run, before the measured Stage E test was tagged slow: **283 tests, 7,875 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**, \"'`target/6db/focused-final.log`. Namespaces: holder driver/export/reader, ledger, authority grant, compose-rows, stage-e-rows, and semantic layout (the first-commit comment). The Stage E body subsequently received only its required `''^:slow` metadata and `slow/guard` wrapper; its unchanged body passed 74 assertions and measured 8.499 s. All other newly measured tests were under 5 s. Per-var evidence: `target/6db/per-var.log`.\n\n| Acceptance item | Result / pass assertions |\n|---|---|\n| Fuel validation, repeated preemption and continuation | `fuel-configuration-and-repeated-boundaries-test`: **14** |\n| Clock cuts (a), (b), (c), (d) | `clock-cuts-retain-the-exact-completed-stage-test`: **144**, nine cuts: before, after slice, inside/after replay, inside/after emit, inside/after read, between slices. Each compares the entire ended machine, pins retained diagnostics/checkpoint/lost local progress, asserts zero serves/attaches/observations and direct-step refusal; a second holder recovers the original checkpoint bytes, with no retained stage marker/control. |\n| Running-root export cuts (e) | `running-export-tenure-cuts-keep-the-exact-fence-test`: **33**, mint/prepare/offer cuts. Entire fence equality, original checkpoint bytes/diagnostic, zero serves/requests after expiry, zero attachments/observations, no resumed report. Stage E separately exercises durable recovery before and after offer. |\n| Running pack publication and successor completion | `running-hand-off-publishes-and-successor-finishes-test`: **8**, running kind, full exit, successor lower/run to 42, stale-source gate refusal |\n| Running offer competitors | `two-candidates-for-a-running-offer-test`: **6**, one machine/holder, loser not-holder with zero attaches, reference completion |\n| Expired running-grant activation | `running-grant-expiry-refuses-before-attachment-test`: **4**, no machine, zero attaches/observations |\n| Running root + wait and running root + ready fenced recovery | `running-products-rehydrate-byte-for-byte-and-refuse-execution-test`: **34**, equal pack bytes, ready retention, all four execution entries refuse “Gate is closed”, zero handle effects, uncertain-offer abort refused in both products |\n| Queue enter/abort retention | `completed-queues-are-retained-without-execution-test`: **5**, order, empty scheduler queue, exact abort machine equality, zero effects |\n| Recovery validation before attachment | existing `recovery-validation-precedes-attachment-test`, extended with ready-count tamper: **44** |\n| Halted-exclusive-root F6 regression | existing `a-halted-result-lowers-without-a-grant-test`: **6** |\n| Existing bare-effect tenure check, strengthened | `tenure-is-rechecked-between-bare-effects-test`: **6**. The old pre-slice child-presence expectation was replaced by exact equality with the completed sweep'\"'s machine: the halted child was already retired before emit lost tenure. The one-permitted-write assertion is unchanged. |\n| Ledger/grant offerability | running ledger **1**, running grant **3**; existing halted refusals also pass in focused suite |\n| Compose boundary hand-off and running install child | \"'`exclusive-fuel-boundary-and-running-install-child-handoff-test`: **15** across pure-running root and real running-initializer child; successor completes, source refuses stepping |\n| Stage E running hand-off, recovery before/after offer, expiry between slices | `running-boundary-handoff-and-expiry-test`: **74**. Final expiry machine equals the entire preceding machine with only the gate ended; recovery is at checkpoint PC 0 instead of retained progressed PC. Pure source/receiver worlds assert zero serves/attaches/observations. |\n| Hold classes / one-cycle behavior | `hold-resolution-needs-acknowledgement-and-backpressure-can-persist-test`: **26**. Observe, held, unminted, link-cursor holds stay refused without authority acknowledgement, then clear after real authority acknowledgement. A full append preserves exact machine equality for ten cycles with one observation. A declared bare pending close resolves in one emit. Non-one-cycle cases are recorded in known gaps. |\n\n**Whole JVM quick tier:** RUNNING; exact result to be filled below. Command `mise exec -- clojure -M:test -e :slow`, log `target/6db/quick.log`. Node REPL built as its prerequisite (225 files, one existing ns-var-clash warning); pinned ANTLR parser generated successfully after retrying the sandbox-blocked download with elevated access. These are prerequisites, not Node/Dart test-lane claims.\n\n**Kondo:** **0 errors, 0 warnings** over every changed Clojure file including first-commit rows/layout (`target/6db/kondo-final.log`); whitespace verification clean. Final slow-wrapper metadata is included in the final lint follow-up.\n\n## Implementation-weakening campaign\n\n`target/6db/mutants.clj`, `target/6db/mutants.log`, `target/6db/mutation-results.edn`: baseline **10 tests, 287 passes, 0 failures/errors**; **13/13 mutants killed**. The campaign precedes the two additional running-product uncertain-abort assertions and Stage E effect-counter assertions; implementation rules are unchanged since the campaign (later source changes are docstrings).\n\n| Mutant | Fail / error |\n|---|---:|\n| fuel runner replaced by unrestricted run | 8 / 1 |\n| tenure guard removed | 28 / 0 |\n| failure reverts to cycle input | 18 / 0 |\n| completed stage discards its machine | 5 / 0 |\n| fuel configuration unchecked | 5 / 0 |\n| running export kind missing | 2 / 0 |\n| ready reinstatement dropped | 13 / 0 |\n| recovery ready count unchecked | 4 / 0 |\n| closed gate unchecked | 25 / 0 |\n| expired tenure treated as holding | 57 / 0 |\n| uncertain-offer abort allowed | 6 / 0 |\n| ledger running offer refused | 3 / 1 |\n| grant running offer refused | 2 / 1 |\n\nBoth new `.cljc` with-redefs sites are gated `:cljd` FIRST, then `:default`, matching the inherited harness discipline. The campaign script is JVM-only under ignored target, not portable test source.\n\n## STOPs, limits, and hygiene\n\n- No design STOP and no protected-pin changes. No assertion was weakened. The child-retirement assertion is stronger full-state equality, matching the required latest-completed-stage semantics.\n- Exact-slice diagnostic unit is called out above and in continuation §7.3; no instruction count or wall-clock guarantee is invented.\n- No Node/Dart lane or three-host slow landing run was performed; those remain the orchestrator'\"'s. The new process test is registered, not claimed executed.\n- No normative clause assigns the kernel guard to 6d-b, forbids supported completed link/install outcomes, validates completed installs against live installs, restarts fuel through maybe-run, or promises one-cycle hold resolution. The old not-quiescent sentence in UCF §7.6.3 is explicitly historical and immediately superseded by its any-pc amendment; there is no runtime holder refusal left.\n- Fable sign-off and merge remain outstanding. The module-export host-function gap and conservative-discharge answer-set drift remain explicit gaps.\n\n## File-to-commit mapping\n\n| Commit / proposed review group | Files |\n|---|---|\n| **262fc609d**, committed first | \"'`docs/agents/known-gaps.md`, `docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc`, `test/yin/vm/semantic/layout_test.cljc` |\n| Holder/custody, uncommitted | `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/{driver,export,reader}.cljc`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/{ledger,compose}.cljc`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority/grant.cljc` |\n| Acceptance tests, uncommitted | `test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/{driver,export,reader}_test.cljc`, `test/yin/vm/ucf/{ledger,compose_rows}_test.cljc`, `test/yin/vm/ucf/authority/grant_test.cljc` |\n| Stage E, uncommitted | `test/yin/vm/ucf/stage_e_{world,scenarios,rows_test}.cljc`, `test/yin/vm/ucf/stage_e_process_test.clj` |\n| Documents, uncommitted | `docs/agents/known-gaps.md`, `docs/design/yin.vm.{semantic.continuation,universal-continuation-format,linker.dht}.md` |\n| Never commit | `collab/` prompt/report, `target/6db/` logs/scripts/results |\n\nPENDING-FINAL-JVM-RESULT\nMD'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
